<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panticapaeum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pantikapaion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Panticapaeum was an ancient Greek city on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch">Kerch</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, founded by colonists from Miletus around 600 BCE. It became the capital of the Bosporan Kingdom, which controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch-strait">Cimmerian Bosporus</a> and exported grain to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> died there in 63 BCE. The remains of its acropolis lie on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-mithridates">Mount Mithridates</a> in the centre of Kerch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panticapaeum.jpg" alt="Panticapaeum" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Derevyagin Igor · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%90%D1%80%D1%85%D1%96%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%BE-%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%85%D0%B5%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%96%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81_%C2%AB%D0%A1%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BD%D1%94_%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE_%D0%9F%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%82%D1%96%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BF%D0%B5%D0%B9%C2%BB.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
